## Home tiles restyled to Databricks Jobs create-tile pattern
================================================================================

Context: After adding the Settings resource card, Home launch tiles still used
tall illustrated cards (SVG art, bullet lists, lift-on-hover). Align them with
the Databricks Jobs create tiles (Ingestion pipeline / ETL Pipeline style) and
the existing Workspace Home MCP card pattern (`.ob-workspace-home-tile`).

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/home.html
   - Launch tiles: icon square + title + count in a head row, short description
     below. Dropped SVG art, bullet lists, and trailing arrows. Icons:
     `bi-layers` (Contexts), `bi-signpost-split` (Bridges), `bi-clipboard-check`
     (My tasks). Count element IDs unchanged for JS.
   - Resource cards: same compact pattern; removed trailing arrows.
2. src/front/static/home/css/home.css
   - Restyle `.home-nav-tile` / `.home-resource-card` to match Workspace Home:
     `--home-tile-radius` (0.5rem), bordered icon square, flat rest, soft
     `0 2px 8px` hover shadow, no translateY / primary-border hover.
3. tests/units/ui/test_home_and_explorer_contracts.py
   - Replaced points-list assertion with
     `test_home_launch_tiles_use_databricks_jobs_card_pattern`.

