## Settings entry point on the Home page
================================================================================

Context: The Home page had no direct way to reach Settings (Databricks warehouse,
graph engine backends, branding, automation runs). Design agreed in brainstorming:
add a "Settings & Config" card to the existing "Keep exploring" resources strip,
next to Help Center. The strip grows from 3 to 4 cards.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/home.html
   - Added `<a class="home-resource-card" href="/settings" data-home-resource="settings">`
     right after the Help Center card. Internal link, same markup as the other cards,
     `bi-arrow-right` affordance (no new tab).
   - Updated the section lead to mention system settings.
2. src/front/static/home/css/home.css
   - `.home-resources-grid`: 4 columns on desktop.
   - Under 991.98px: 2 columns (tablet). Existing <768px rule keeps 1 column.
3. tests/units/ui/test_home_and_explorer_contracts.py
   - `test_home_resources_strip_links_to_settings`: card links to /settings, is
     same-tab, and has no external-link affordance.
   - `test_home_resources_grid_is_four_columns_on_desktop`: pins the 4 / 2 column
     grid rules.

