## Configurable Databricks button styles: Create (filled) and Share (outlined)
================================================================================

Context: The Databricks Catalog browse page uses two button styles: Create
(solid primary) and Share (outlined secondary). OntoBricks now exposes both in
Settings → Configuration → UI → Theme, defaulting to the Databricks values and
letting an admin change the colours. Applied to page buttons (`.btn-primary` =
Create, `.btn-secondary` / `.btn-outline-secondary` = Share) and to the navbar
chrome: Save = Create, Close = Share, Resume editing stays a warning ghost.
Blank or invalid stored colours fall back to the Databricks defaults.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/helpers/UIBranding.py
   - `DEFAULT_BUTTON_PRIMARY_COLOR` (#2272B4) and `DEFAULT_BUTTON_SECONDARY_COLOR`
     (#11171C); Databricks companion tints (`DATABRICKS_CREATE_HOVER`,
     `DATABRICKS_SHARE_BORDER`, `DATABRICKS_SHARE_HOVER`) used exactly for defaults.
   - `BrandPalette` gains `button_primary`, `button_primary_hover`,
     `button_on_primary`, `button_secondary`, `button_secondary_border`,
     `button_secondary_hover`; `UIBranding` gains `button_primary_color` and
     `button_secondary_color`.
   - New `derive_button_palette()`; `derive_brand_palette()` and
     `normalize_ui_branding()` accept and resolve the two colours.
2. src/back/core/helpers/__init__.py
   - Re-exports the two default constants.
3. src/shared/fastapi/ui_branding.py
   - `render_ui_branding_css_vars` emits `--db-btn-primary`, `-hover`, `-on`,
     `--db-btn-secondary`, `-border`, `-hover` into `#uiBrandingTokens`.
4. src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
   - Persists `button_primary_color` / `button_secondary_color` in `ui_branding`;
     `_empty()` defaults updated.
5. src/back/objects/domain/settings/WorkspaceUiSettings.py
   - `save_ui_branding_result` takes the two colours (keyword, default blank),
     validates them, and persists the normalized values.
6. src/back/objects/domain/settings/SettingsService.py
   - Facade forwards the two colours (kept on one line to stay within the
     `SettingsService` size baseline).
7. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   - `POST /ui-branding` accepts `button_primary_color` and `button_secondary_color`
     form fields.
8. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   - `:root` defaults for the six `--db-btn-*` tokens.
   - `.ob-subnav-save-btn` → Create (solid); `.ob-subnav-save-kbd` on Create label colour;
     `.ob-subnav-close-btn` → Share (white surface, border, hover tint).
9. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   - `.btn-primary` → solid Create (`--db-btn-primary`), no gradient, no resting shadow.
   - `.btn-secondary` / `.btn-outline-secondary` → Share block (white surface at
     rest, `--db-btn-secondary-border`, hover `--db-btn-secondary-hover`, focus ring);
     removed from the neutral and outline lists.
10. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   - `UI_BRANDING_DEFAULTS` gains the two colours and the six palette keys.
   - `deriveButtonPalette()` mirrors the Python derivation (verified numerically
     identical for default and custom colours); `deriveBrandPalette()` takes the
     two colours; `draftPalette()` keeps them across primary/Aurora edits.
   - `normalizeUIBrandingDraft()` builds the palette from one fallback object.
   - Preview sets the `--db-btn-*` variables; validity, dirty state, saved-default
     check, input sync, blur handling and the save `FormData` cover both colours.
11. src/front/templates/settings.html
   - Theme card: "Create button color" and "Share button color" pickers (colour +
     hex + help + error) after Aurora; preview gains a Share sample button.
12. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   - Documents the Create/Share tokens, derivation rules, the navbar mapping, and
     the updated button hierarchy/states; `--db-gradient-primary` marked unused.
13. tests/units/front/test_button_design_contract.py
   - Share focus keeps the white surface (`var(--db-surface-warm)`) as its resting
     background, in addition to `transparent`.
14. tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py
   - `.btn-primary` asserts Create tokens and no shadow; `.btn-secondary` and
     `.btn-outline-secondary` assert the white surface token.
15. tests/units/front/test_segmented_subnav_contract.py
   - Renamed to `test_chrome_actions_use_create_and_share_styles`; asserts Save =
     Create and Close = Share, with their hover tints.
16. tests/units/settings/test_v090_settings_workspace_ui.py
   - Exact-dict persistence assertion includes the two colours; new tests for
     explicit, blank and invalid Create colours.
17. tests/units/ui/test_ui_button_styles.py (new)
   - Databricks default palette is exact; custom colours derive companions;
     invalid stored colours fall back; CSS variables are published.
18. tests/units/front/test_ui_button_styles_contract.py (new)
   - Settings pickers, preview sample, JS payload and preview variables, and
     `main.css` / `components.css` token contracts.

Design notes:
- Navbar Save (filled) and Close (outlined) reverse the earlier borderless /
  no-background-at-rest chrome for those two buttons. This is the approved
  content_and_chrome option; Resume editing is unchanged.
- `--db-gradient-primary` is no longer used by any component. It is kept because
  the contract tests assert the token; remove it in a follow-up.

