## Apply Create/Share button paint to every Bootstrap action variant
================================================================================

Context: Create and Share were wired for `.btn-primary` / `.btn-secondary` /
`.btn-outline-secondary`, but ~127 `btn-outline-primary` usages (and the
success/warning/info/light/dark solid and outline classes) still used the old
neutral grey outline. The app now has only two button looks everywhere:
Create (filled) and Share (outlined), including Studio / graph toolbars that
already use those Bootstrap classes. Destructive keeps Share structure with
danger colours; `.btn-link` stays text-only.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   - Folded `.btn-outline-primary`, `.btn-success`, `.btn-warning`, `.btn-info`,
     `.btn-light`, `.btn-dark` and their outline forms into the Share selector
     family (same `--db-btn-secondary*` tokens, white surface, hover tint).
   - `.btn-danger` joins `.btn-outline-danger` as the destructive Share paint
     (red label/border, soft-danger hover, white surface at rest/focus).
   - Removed the old transparent/neutral outline blocks those variants used.
2. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   - Documents the universal Create/Share mapping and the danger exception.
3. tests/units/front/test_button_design_contract.py
   - Share-family focus contract covers the expanded list; danger focus keeps
     the red label for both `.btn-danger` and `.btn-outline-danger`.
4. tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py
   - `.btn-outline-primary` asserts the Share white surface token.
5. tests/units/front/test_ui_button_styles_contract.py
   - New resting-paint contract: outline-primary uses Share surface + border.

